---
import BaseLayout from '../../layouts/BaseLayout.astro';
import { site } from '../../data/site';
---
<BaseLayout title="Contribute" description="Find PlayMAKER repositories, share feedback and contribute as projects become available." path="/contribute/">
  <section class="page-hero"><div class="shell"><p class="eyebrow">Build with us</p><h1>Better tools are<br />a team effort.</h1><p class="section-lede">Designers, developers, coaches, analysts and club volunteers all see different problems. Help us make the tools useful for the people doing the work.</p></div></section>
  <section class="page-section"><div class="shell"><div class="content-grid"><div class="panel"><p class="section-kicker">01 / Explore</p><h2>Find the work</h2><p>Start at the <a class="inline-link" href={site.orgUrl} target="_blank" rel="noopener noreferrer">PlayMAKER GitHub organization</a>. Repositories are published as projects become ready for collaboration.</p></div><div class="panel"><p class="section-kicker">02 / Share</p><h2>Open a useful issue</h2><p>In a repository that accepts Issues, describe the team workflow, what happened, what you expected and a small way to reproduce the problem. Use available labels when present.</p></div><div class="panel"><p class="section-kicker">03 / Build</p><h2>Contribute code or docs</h2><p>Read the repository's contribution guide and license before a pull request. This site has its own development and deployment instructions in the README.</p></div><div class="panel"><p class="section-kicker">04 / Respect</p><h2>Work well together</h2><p>Follow the <a class="inline-link" href="#conduct">community code of conduct</a>. Discussions and issue labels are only available where maintainers enable them.</p></div></div><div class="copy-section"><h2 id="guide">Contribution guide</h2><p>Choose an open repository and read its README, license and current Issues. For this website, run <code>npm ci</code>, <code>npm run build</code> and <code>npm test</code> before a pull request. Explain the club problem your change solves, and include screenshots for visual changes. Keep links and release statuses accurate in <code>src/data/site.ts</code>.</p><h2 id="conduct">Community code of conduct</h2><p>Be respectful and specific. Welcome contributors across sports, skill levels and backgrounds. Critique ideas and code without personal attacks, harassment or discriminatory language. Maintainers may remove abusive contributions or restrict participation.</p><p>For a conduct concern, contact a repository maintainer through an available private GitHub contact channel. If one is not listed, ask for a private contact route without posting sensitive details in a public issue.</p></div><div class="callout"><p>No community forum or public Discussions space is configured in this site's data yet. Use the linked GitHub repositories for feedback where their Issues are enabled.</p></div></div></section>
</BaseLayout>
